---
name: Auth-Readiness Query Gate
description: RLS-gated hooks must wait for auth bootstrap before querying to avoid empty-cache race
type: preference
---
RLS-gated React Query hooks (anything depending on auth.uid()) MUST gate `enabled` on `isReady && !!user` from `useAuth()`, not just on input params.

Why: cold mounts can fire PostgREST requests before Supabase rehydrates the session from localStorage. Without a token, RLS returns 0 rows and React Query caches the empty result for the staleTime, requiring a manual refresh to recover.

How to apply:
1. `const { isReady, user } = useAuth();`
2. `enabled: isReady && !!user && <other gates>`
3. Include `user?.id` in the query key so cache is per-user.
4. AuthContext invalidates `org-level-kpis*`, `org-kpi-values`, `org-kpi-data-owners*`, `org-kpi-data-owner-names`, `org-kpi-owners`, `org-kpi-owner-check`, `kpis*`, `my-kpis` on the not-ready → ready transition to evict any caches that raced (defence-in-depth).

Reference: ADR-052, POLICY §96. Triggered by Chandan Pandit (Org KPI Data Entry blank-until-refresh bug, May 2026).
